keywords:
  - brain evolution
  - cooperative breeding
  - life history
  - human childhood
  - phylogenetic comparative methods
  - Piantadosi and Kidd model
abstract: >-
  Reproducibility package for a study that reproduces the Piantadosi and Kidd (2016)
  runaway selection model of human intelligence, extends it with a single shared-care
  term, derives in closed form that the private survival benefit of parental intelligence
  scales as the inverse square of total care, calibrates the effect dimensionlessly,
  validates the simulation against a reference implementation, reanalyzes the supporting
  cross-species correlation with phylogenetic methods, and places the result against
  hominin fossil evidence on body mass, brain size, and helpless infancy.
